    <h1 style="font-size: 36pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">Research Update</h1>

    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">Spring Workshops Cover All Aspects of Research</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">March and April were a busy couple of months for the Research Services staff. We were excited to offer several workshops for faculty, students, and staff, including grant management, proposal writing, and an introduction to technology transfer and intellectual property.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">The Grant Management Workshop in March brought together representatives from ORS, the Graduate School, sponsored research accounting, Human Resources, Corporate and Foundation Relations, and Faculty Administration. The group taught faculty and business administrators about a wide range of grant management responsibilities.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">The Proposal Writing Workshop was run by Dr. Robert Lucas, the director of Institute for Scholarly Productivity and a <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span>.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 40px;">
        <div style="width: 30%;">
            <div class="section-heading">Inside this issue:</div>
            <div class="list-item">ORS Staff News <span data-field="ors_staff_news_count">{{ ors_staff_news_count }}</span></div>
            <div class="list-item">Student Re-search High-lights <span data-field="student_highlights_count">{{ student_highlights_count }}</span></div>
            <div class="list-item">News from the Centers of Excellence <span data-field="centers_of_excellence_count">{{ centers_of_excellence_count }}</span></div>
            <div class="list-item">Federal Agency Announcements <span data-field="federal_announcements_count">{{ federal_announcements_count }}</span></div>
            <div class="list-item">New Internal Award for Col-laborations <span data-field="internal_awards_count">{{ internal_awards_count }}</span></div>
            <div class="list-item">Focus on Teaching <span data-field="teaching_focus_count">{{ teaching_focus_count }}</span></div>
            <div class="list-item">Recent Awards <span data-field="recent_awards_count">{{ recent_awards_count }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 65%;">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 10px;">
                <div style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">"Teacher-Scholar" the Focus at Academic Research Forum</div>
                <div style="font-size: 10pt;">See "Workshops" on page 3.</div>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">The Academic Research Forum has grown into a key annual event for faculty who want to meet and interact with other faculty members from across the university. This year's event focused on the challenges and re-wards of being an effective teacher-scholar.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Dr. Art Lungo facilitated a faculty panel, which featured Dr. Anthony Burrow, psychology; Dr. Allen Frantzen, eng-lish; Dr. Catherine Putonti, biology and computer science; and Dr. Elizabeth Vera, School of Education, counseling psychology.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Each panel member talked about the specific ways in which he or she inte-grates research and teaching and en-</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">ouraged questions from the audience about implementing the ideas into their classes and pro-jects.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">As always, the fo-rum provided a unique and valuable opportunity for fac-ulty members to learn from others in different disciplines and to foster inter-disciplinary connec-tions.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

