        <div style="width: 65%;">
            <div class="section-heading">Loyola Students Enrich Classroom Learning with Research</div>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">ORS was excited to be a part of the 2010 Undergraduate Research Symposium. More than 160 students presented their projects, most of which were conducted through one of the LUROP fellowships.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Several students in the Graduate School have obtained external awards in recog-nition of their superior work. Alec Lucas, a PhD candidate in philosophy was hon-ored with a prestigious Fulbright fellow-ship.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Lucas will travel to Heidelberg University in Germany in order to enrich his disser-tation work in New Testament studies. You can read more about his work in the Loyola Phoenix (http://www.loyolaphx.com/).</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Any graduate students in a PhD program who are interested in external funding, should contact Dr. Jessica Horowitz (jhorow@luc.edu) in the Graduate School for guidance and to discuss the internal RIAGS funding opportunity.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

