    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <div class="sub-heading">Writing and provided concrete writing and time management tips.</div>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">ORS director, Bill Sellers, spearheaded the event "Applying the Fruits of Your Re-search" the first-ever forum at Loyola to focus on the ways in which innovators can be utilized for the public good and provide tangible benefits to inventors.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Approximately 25 faculty from the lake-side and Maywood campuses spent the day listening to presentations and panel discussions by lawyers, consultants, and industry executives, who also spent time answering questions and engaging in dis-cussions about future opportunities for Loyola faculty inventors. Questions about the event or technology transfer should be directed to Bill Sellers (wsellers@luc.edu).</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <div class="sub-heading">ORS also co-sponsored several events this spring. April 23 was the 3rd Annual Academic Research Forum, put together with the Center for Faculty Professional Development. More details on that event can be found on the first page of the newsletter. We were also pleased to help plan an expanded version of the under-graduate research symposium. More de-tails on that event can be found on page 2.</div>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Looking ahead, ORS anticipates partici-pating in the Focus on Teaching event, to be held on August 19. (Details on page 4).</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Information on upcoming and past events can be found here: http://www.luc.edu/ors/ NewsandEvents.shtml.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <div class="section-heading">Federal Agency Announcements</div>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">As part of an initiative to ensure more ef-fective sharing of research data, the Na-tional Science Foundation announced that, as of October 2010, a 2-page data management plan will become a required supplement for all proposals. Details will be released closer to October.</p>
            <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
                <div style="font-size: 10pt; color: #888;">+++</div>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">As of August 10, The National Institutes of Health will require that SNAP progress</p>
