        <div style="width: 65%;">
            <div class="section-heading">New Internal Award for Cross-Campus Collaboration</div>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Loyola's most recent internal funding opportunity, the President's Intercampus Collaborative Research Stimulus Award, has garnered a significant response in its inaugural funding year. The awards, developed to provide seed funding for innovative research projects that cross campus boundaries, are available to faculty from across the university.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">The deadline for this year's submission was May 3, and although a winning team was hoped to be announced by August 1, there may be a slight delay due to the unanticipated number of proposals received.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">The Research Services staff at Maywood and lakeside are enthusiastic about this new initiative and look forward to sharing news about the winning proposal and the exciting research being undertaken among the Loyola's three campuses.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">For more information on the President's Intercampus Collaborative Research Stimulus Award, please visit http://www.luc.edu/ors/pdfs/Research/ ResCollabUCmemo.doc.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px; background-color: #f9f9f9;">
                <div style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Focus on Teaching</div>
                <div style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 5px;">The Many Faces of Diversity at Loyola University Chicago</div>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 10px;">Thursday, August 19, 2010, Lakeshore Campus</p>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Featuring keynote speaker Dr. Beau Basel Beaudoin, Coordinator, Culture, Race and Media, Columbia College; 2009-10 Distinguished Teaching Fel-low, Carnegie Foundation Illinois Professor of the Year. A Focus on Learn-ing will discuss challenges of working with diverse students with the empha-sis from a learning styles perspective.</p>
                <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
                    <div style="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold;">Call for Proposals:</div>
                    <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">The event will feature a series of breakout sessions led by Loyola faculty. We encourage you to submit a proposal that deals with some aspect of diver-sity in our classrooms or on our campus. Poster submissions are also wel-come.</p>
                    <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Please visit http://www.luc.edu/learningtech/FOT2.shtml for more information.</p>
                    <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">Research Services hopes to sponsor another breakout session this year; please look for the final schedule for details.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
